agents mcp add — Add or update a workspace MCP server and sync

USAGE
  agents mcp add <name> <commandOrUrl> [args...] [options]

ARGUMENTS
  <name> <commandOrUrl> [args...]  Server name, executable or URL, and forwarded server arguments.

OPTIONS
  -H value
    	header alias
  -account string
    	account identifier for placeholder replacement
  -dir string
    	workspace directory containing .mcp.json (default ".")
  -e value
    	env alias
  -env value
    	environment variable in KEY=value format (repeatable)
  -header value
    	HTTP header in 'Header: Value' format (repeatable)
  -no-sync
    	skip synchronizing native harness configuration files
  -t string
    	transport type alias
  -type string
    	transport type: stdio or http (auto-detected if omitted)
  -h, --help
    Show this help and exit.

DEFAULTS
  Transport is inferred from the command or URL. Options must precede name; following arguments are forwarded unchanged.

ENVIRONMENT
  MCP_CONNECTOR_ACCOUNT: fallback for -account when synchronizing.

EXAMPLES
  agents mcp add -e MODE=local example npx -y example-server
